{
 "_": "Body shape sliders for the B1 character bodies (design/godot-characters.md). Each slider is made of one or two blend shapes: '<name>+' (slider > 0) and '<name>-' (slider < 0); a 0..1 slider has only '<name>+'. A side is either a MakeHuman macro change ('macro': parameters set relative to the body's defaults; the blend shape is the exact difference) or plain targets ('targets': [[path, weight]]). 'scale' multiplies the side. 'sex' limits a slider to one body. Correctives ('correct') are exact MakeHuman interaction terms between macro sliders, weighted at runtime by the product of the named sides (e.g. weight+ x muscle+). Skeleton-only sliders (posture) have 'bones' instead of shapes: rest rotations (degrees, about the bone's own X) times the slider.",
